course: dictionary
lesson: 15943
title: Un- means not
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: The prefix un- at the start of a word means not. So unsheared means not sheared. Sheared means the wool has been cut off a sheep, so an unsheared sheep still has all its wool. «The unsheared sheep had thick, woolly coats.» The clue is the un-, and the rest of the word tells you the rest of the meaning.
explain: Check your meaning by swapping it into the sentence. «The not sheared sheep had thick, woolly coats» still makes sense, so you are right. You can use the same trick with other words that start with un-, such as unlock (not lock) or unhappy (not happy).
explain: Unsheared is also a maths word. «The farmer had 50 sheep. 30 were sheared, so 20 were unsheared.» Total minus sheared gives unsheared: 50 − 30 = 20. Look for the words sheared and unsheared in a question and work out which numbers to take away.
fact: The prefix un- means not, so unsheared means not sheared.
fact: «Unsheared» means the sheep still has its wool, because it has not been cut.
fact: «Shear» means to cut the wool off a sheep, and a «shearer» is the person who does it.
fact: «Shorn» describes a sheep that has already been sheared.
fact: In maths, unsheared = total − sheared: if 40 sheep are in the field and 25 are sheared, then 15 are unsheared.
exercise: «The unsheared sheep had thick, woolly coats.» What does unsheared mean? | Wet from the rain | Lost in the field | Sheared, with the wool cut off | *Not cut, still with its wool
exercise: A farm has 40 sheep. 25 of them are sheared. How many are unsheared? | *15 | 25 | 65 | 40
exercise: What does «shear» mean? | To wash the sheep's face | To feed the sheep at night | *To cut the wool off a sheep | To count the sheep in a field
test: What does the prefix un- mean at the start of a word? | Again | Before | Very | *Not
test: Which sheep is unsheared? | A sheep that has been shorn | A sheep with a red mark on its back | *A sheep with its thick wool still on | A sheep whose wool was just cut
exam: «The farmer counted 60 sheep: 45 were sheared and the rest were unsheared.» How many sheep were unsheared? | *15 | 105 | 60 | 45
